WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.730
In 1859, Tyndall showed that some
gases block infrared radiation.

2
00:00:05.780 --> 00:00:11.170
In 1896, Arrhenius published the first
calculation of global warming from human

3
00:00:11.220 --> 00:00:13.110
emissions of CO₂.

4
00:00:13.160 --> 00:00:17.190
In 1960, Keeling measured CO₂
in the atmosphere accurately,

5
00:00:17.240 --> 00:00:19.950
and detected an annual rise.

6
00:00:20.000 --> 00:00:24.350
Yet a century after Arrhenius,
it was still being argued over.

7
00:00:24.400 --> 00:00:25.270
Why?

8
00:00:25.320 --> 00:00:27.670
Was the early science simply wrong?

9
00:00:27.720 --> 00:00:30.170
In this mission, you'll trace the science,

10
00:00:30.220 --> 00:00:33.190
from early physics to
measuring and modelling.

11
00:00:33.240 --> 00:00:35.390
Then you'll weigh the
roles of governments,

12
00:00:35.440 --> 00:00:40.250
the UN, the EU, the press,
business and campaign groups.

13
00:00:40.300 --> 00:00:45.390
Your mission: explain why the link between
carbon dioxide and warming was still

14
00:00:45.440 --> 00:00:47.570
argued over a century later.
